The platform team's approved extension is included. The world now imports `http-client` alongside `state-rw`, and every call fetches the enrichment record. The fetch uses `fetch`, so a transport failure comes back as a value and is discarded, and the output does not depend on it.

`PublishedDigest` has no field called "text", so I used `date` as the query value, percent-encoded. If you meant a different field, change the `q` argument.

I also guessed at when ids get recorded: they are marked seen only when `published` is true. An unpublished digest records nothing and returns `recorded: 0`.

